From: Codex Executor <codex-executor@local>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 11:32:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 08/22] Sheet route: symmetry-invariant active carrier set,
 float32 upper-triangle labels, N x N x N block and rotation checks,
 population generator

- active carrier set: the carrier triangulation is not invariant under the cube symmetries (one diagonal per square,
  clipped traces on cut faces), so "vertices of the triangles the band reaches" gave a cell and its symmetry image
  different active sets.  New rule (equivariant_active_nodes): a node is active iff a closed carrier square containing
  it is reached by the band on a symmetric cell-centred face lattice; carrier_active_set (cap constraints) uses the
  same lattice, so the node set contains every vertex of every constraint triangle by construction.  carrier_n is
  passed explicitly through build_sheet_solid_surface / compile_port.
- labels stored as the float32 upper triangle (q(q+1)/2 entries, 64 MB at q = 5643) with the P1 mass and
  Laplace-Beltrami matrices as COO; sheet_label_pipeline.load_schur / load_carrier_norms rebuild them; the gates are
  evaluated in float64 before storage
- sheet_block_validation.py generalized to --shape Nx Ny Nz (eight-cell assembly validation); sheet_rotation_check.py
  labels a cell and its symmetry image independently and compares the transformed operator on the common active
  nodes; make_sheet_population.py (Sobol population, corner spread <= 0.47)
